+# (4b) install-script unwiring negative controls. The legacy fallback
+#     answered True for an install-script patch even after its mount +
+#     invoke were STRIPPED from the compose (its markers — a bare
+#     install.sh, the parent-dir name "patches" — matched any compose that
+#     mounts or runs ANY install-script patch), and a target-only volume
+#     check counts a DIFFERENT patch mounted at the same in-container
+#     target. For every install-script patch with a declared mount target:
+#     a stripped fixture must read not-reached, a different-patch-same-
+#     target fixture must read not-reached, and the patch's own wiring
+#     (positive control) must read reached — otherwise the two negatives
+#     could both pass as a degenerate always-False.
+_install_patches = [
+    p for p in patches
+    if (p.get("delivery") or {}).get("entrypoint_invoke")
+    and p.get("delivery_mechanism") == "install_script"
+    and (p.get("delivery_spec") or {}).get("mounted_at")
+]
